WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.055 --> 00:00:09.215
 

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.680
For me, the most important thing is the story that I'm telling.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.900
whether it's a scary set piece, or a dramatic moment,

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.660
It all comes down to the character

00:00:20.095 --> 00:00:21.245
and if you care about them

00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:29.165
Aquaman is very powerful,

00:00:29.885 --> 00:00:32.925
But what drives him comes from a very human place.

00:00:33.675 --> 00:00:35.875
The story resonated with me instantly.

00:00:37.655 --> 00:00:39.945
He's not accepted here, not really accepted here..

00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:41.965
Definitely can identify with that.

00:00:43.485 --> 00:00:46.245
I fell in love with the project, and fell in love with Mera.

00:00:47.845 --> 00:00:48.945
She's no damsel in distress.

00:00:50.235 --> 00:00:53.600
She's this strong, badass, empowered superhero.

00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:03.105
With Aquaman, the trick and also part of the fun

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:06.160
is designing this whole world that we've never seen before.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.500
You're pretty much just limited by your own imagination.

00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:13.025
There's just a whole lot of magic in this project.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.540
Once they put all these things together behind James's vision,

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.840
Blows my mind still.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.320
The appeal of it was to step into something else.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.680
You really are invigorated because of it.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.300
You get to experience all these amazing worlds.

00:01:29.725 --> 00:01:32.375
We haven't been under the ocean yet.  This is our outer space.

00:01:36.175 --> 00:01:40.500
I keep going back to that inherent fascination we have with the ocean.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.345
...and if it turned on you.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.880
Just the sheer vastness and the mystery of it

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.560
There's still a lot we don't know.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.920
I've always known that I wanted to do an action movie.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.695
I get to be a big kid on the playground, and cause trouble.

00:01:55.695 --> 00:01:56.695
...blow things up.

00:01:57.955 --> 00:02:00.065
Your body is constantly working.

00:02:00.695 --> 00:02:03.205
Judo, Jiujitsu, fight choreography.

00:02:05.295 --> 00:02:06.295
After 4.5 months of stunt training,

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:07.785
6 days a week...

00:02:09.015 --> 00:02:10.425
you feel pretty superhuman.

00:02:12.235 --> 00:02:15.295
I get to present Aquaman to the world in this really

00:02:15.365 --> 00:02:17.635
baddass and cool way.

00:02:19.075 --> 00:02:21.305
We have never seen this on screen.

00:02:21.745 --> 00:02:23.635
That's the truth.

00:02:26.215 --> 00:02:29.485
You get to fall in love with the idea of what it's like to have these powers...and be a kid.

00:02:29.625 --> 00:02:31.445
And that's fun for the family.  It's fun for everyone.

00:02:32.355 --> 00:02:34.580
We want to create something interesting.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:35.580
We don't want the standard.

00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:38.100
James Wong can't do the standard.

00:02:42.185 --> 00:02:45.595
Any great superhero story should make you feel

00:02:45.595 --> 00:02:47.835
that you've learned something from these characters.

00:02:49.445 --> 00:02:52.365
And you yourself have the ability to do good.

00:02:55.785 --> 00:02:58.025
And you don't need a cape to be able to do that.

